## Usage

This is a generic workspace: it ships almost nothing on purpose. Use it for whatever the
project needs — drafting documents under `docs/`, keeping notes, or writing throwaway
scripts — with Python, `uv`, `ruff` and `pytest` already available inside the devcontainer.

```console
$ uv run python              # a REPL in the project environment
$ uv add <package>           # add a dependency
```

## Development

```console
$ uv run pytest         # run the test suite (does nothing until tests/ has tests)
$ uv run ruff check .   # lint
$ uv run ruff format .  # format
```

`pyproject.toml` sets `[tool.uv] package = false`, so there is nothing to build or publish.
If the workspace turns into a real Python package, add a `[build-system]` and a
`src/<package>/` layout, or re-run `cdforge adopt` on the host and pick the `python_uv_tool`
type.
